From ad0b11bcfdfacf4f0b50beb5ff421192087df727 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:34:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iowave: cache relaxation-zone geometry for slice4 relaxation
 loops

distgen()/distbeach() (and xgen()/ygen()) tested every slice cell
against all B107/B108 zone polygons on every call, 6+ times per FNPF
step. The zones and the grid are fixed, so iowave::relaxzone4_build()
now stores the cells that lie in a generation or beach zone once (in
SLICELOOP4 order, with their distances), and the loops visit only those.
Cells outside both zones were never modified by these loops.

Converted: eta_relax, wm_relax, ws_relax, pm_relax (iowave_sflow_relax),
fifsf_relax, test_relax, fnpf_precalc_relax,
wavegen_precalc_decomp_relax_fnpf.

3D irregular case, 250x250x10, 1 rank, 100 steps:
  relax            1.24 s -> 0.13 s
  wavegen_precalc  2.46 s -> 2.03 s
Gauge output byte-identical to hans_dev on the 1- and 2-rank 3D
irregular cases, the 3D bathymetry case with 5 B107/B108 zones on
2 ranks, and the 2D submerged bar on 2 ranks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MepgQUKXTT5xXWWgdAkDNj
